Convert MCP tools into LLM tool schemas
The MCP server returns tools with this general structure:
tool.nametool.descriptiontool.inputSchema



Your OpenRouter API expects a structure like this:
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "divide",
    "description": "Divide the first number by the second number.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "a": {"type": "number"},
        "b": {"type": "number"}
      },
      "required": ["a", "b"]
    }
  }
}


The important mapping is:
MCP tool field	LLM API field
tool.name	function.name
tool.description	function.description
tool.inputSchema	function.parameters



So the client transforms the MCP definition into the format OpenRouter expects.
Why do this? Because MCP and the LLM API use different interfaces for describing tools. Your client acts as the adapter between them.

